# Half-Life RPG. Measured by vrcardgen, finished by hand.
#
# Part J: "Slide a rocket into the tube until it latches. Shoulder it."
#
# ONE ROUND AND NO ACTION. There is nothing on this launcher for a hand to
# work: no bolt, no magazine, no cover. The rocket is the entire loading
# gesture, so the card declares no joints at all and the weapon loads at the
# port - which `single_shot` does without needing an action joint, and
# without `needs_cock`, because an RPG has no sear to set.
#
# The generator reports the `Rocket` bone travelling ten thousand units. That
# is not a measurement of a mechanism, it is the rocket leaving: the launch
# animation flies it away from the weapon. The tool already classifies it as
# an object arriving from outside rather than a joint, which is exactly right
# - the feed path owns the rocket, and where the animation throws it is of no
# interest to anybody.
#
# `Cylinder01` exists, owns 2.5% of the mesh and is never animated. It is a
# candidate for a declared travel later - the plan's laser sight housing -
# but nobody has measured one, so it stays undeclared and keeps behaving as
# it does today.

weapon v_rpg
match  bones 54  seqs 9  hash 0x58602f2c

type   single_shot  rpm 150
# The rate is deliberately loose. On a weapon like this the MECHANISM is the
# limiter - you cannot shoot faster than you can work it and lay the next one
# in - so a low rpm only adds a second, invisible timer that stops the weapon
# firing when the player has done everything right. It is here to keep two
# shots out of one millisecond, and nothing more.
